<metadata><name>NYYC 172nd Annual Regatta - Navigator Courses 1 and 2</name><desc>New York Yacht Club 172nd Annual Regatta, 12-14 June 2026, Sailing Instructions incorporating Amendment 1, SI Addendum A (Courses using Government Marks) A2.4 and A2.5. Course is shown on a board on the RC signal vessel no later than the warning signal (number 1 or 2) and normally announced on the circle VHF channel. Start: RC line in the rendezvous area signalled ashore that day (SI 3.3, 6) - no fixed start position is published, so the route is drawn from the Fort Adams line (approx). Finish: off Fort Adams between a blue flag on an RC vessel and the finishing mark, approximately 0.4 NM north of Fl R 6s Horn 2 (Fort Adams Light 2). Cautions: both bridges must be passed through the center span only (the piers are a gate, A2.1); pass to the west of R12 off Rose Island; the RC may add a set Special Mark E as a new first mark (A3.6, not drawn); if flag F is flown at the start the finish moves to about 1 NM bearing 310 from Fort Adams Light 2 (A2.9, not drawn); Navy security zone north of the Pell Bridge on the Newport shore (SI 18.2). Courses 3 and 4 are mark lists posted on the day and are not included. Jamestown bridge point is chart-approximate. No distance is published; drawn length is about 19.2 NM.</desc></metadata>
<wpt lat="41.48841" lon="-71.33677"><name>RC line 0.4 NM N of Fort Adams Light 2 (approx)</name><sym>Buoy</sym></wpt>
